# =============================================================================
# .gitignore - solar-potential-toolkit
# =============================================================================
# This is a multi-country pipeline; raw input data (rasters and
# administrative vectors) is intentionally NOT stored or redistributed in
# this repository, primarily because some source datasets carry licensing
# or redistribution restrictions (GADM: academic/non-commercial use only,
# redistribution requires prior permission - see LICENSE and each
# config/<country>.json's "provenance" block for full per-source terms).
#
# Users must obtain the raw datasets themselves from their respective
# providers; acquisition instructions and exact per-country provenance are
# documented in data/raster/README.md, data/vectors/README.md, and
# config/*.json.
#
# Rerunning scripts/run_pipeline.py locally regenerates everything under
# outputs/ from data/ + config/ + scripts/ + utils/ - that reproducibility
# is the point of not tracking outputs/ either.
# =============================================================================

# --- Raw input data (not redistributed) -------------------------------------
data/raster/*
!data/raster/README.md
data/vectors/*
!data/vectors/README.md

# --- Pipeline outputs (regenerated by scripts/00 -> 04) ---------------------
outputs/

# --- Python virtual environments --------------------------------------------
# No bare "env/" or "ENV/" rule here: on Windows, Git's case-insensitive
# filesystem matching means "ENV/" would also match "env/" (the credentials
# subfolder containing env/.env.example, which must stay tracked) - this was
# verified directly: `git check-ignore -v env/.env.example` matched "ENV/"
# before ever reaching the intended env/.env rule below, meaning the
# template file was being silently excluded. This project's Python
# environment is managed via conda (`conda create -n solar_toolkit ...`),
# stored outside the repo, so a local venv folder is not expected here anyway.
.venv/
venv/
.conda/

# --- Python caches and compiled files ---------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/

# --- Jupyter / Spyder --------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.spyproject/
.spyderworkspace

# --- IDE / editors -----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- OS-specific files --------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Temporary files and logs -------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak

# --- Credentials / secrets (security) ------------------------------------------
# Only env/.env (real credentials) is ignored - env/.env.example is the
# tracked template and must stay versioned, so it is explicitly excluded
# from this rule by not being matched at all (path-qualified, not a bare
# ".env" pattern that would ambiguously apply repo-wide).
env/.env
*.pem
secrets.yaml
